{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a metallaphotocatalytic method for the directed ortho-hydroxylation of substituted anilides. By combining the organo-photocatalyst 4CzIPN with a ruthenium transition metal catalyst [RuCl2(p-cymene)]2 and the hypervalent iodine(III) oxidant PIFA, the authors achieved site-selective C-H oxidation under mild visible-light conditions. The method is particularly effective for substrates with electron-withdrawing groups and was applied to the synthesis of stable-isotope-labeled 3-hydroxy anthranilic acid.",
